mantle rm362
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_florence_millhand
title the straw tide gauge
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk leaves_a_straw_in_the_gutter_to_measure_the_first_rise
likes plum_tart roof_birds fresh_straw misty_dawns
dislikes deep_mud night_noise
fears a_closed_purse_at_the_new_moon
hopes a_dry_road_to_a_better_wage
topics work +0.6 weather +0.5 dreams +0.4 prices +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=sparing refuse=careful tease=none
marks oath saying
persona persona #self.first# sets a bright straw at the rising edge of a gutter and measures every walk against a private date.

words
oath! = Float my last straw | Drown the short measure
saying! = Rising water brings its own measuring rod | The high road starts where your feet are
straw = a clean pale stem | a yellow straw
mark = a bit of brick dust | a chalk nick
gutter = a narrow runnel | a broad gutter
wing = a little roof wing | a flicking wingtip
mist = a hanging mist | a thin dawn haze
tart = a crooked bit of tart | a pastry crescent
cart = a cargo cart | a low truck
lip = a shelf of stone | a dry stone lip
coin = a saved halfpenny | a worn copper
moonedge = a fine silver edge | a slender moon
sling = a rough carrying sling | a square of worn canvas
curb = a low kerb | a broken kerb
jar = a lidded stone jar | a squat pot

any
opinion houses against 2 : A factor's calendar doesn't get any heavier as the date draws near. The weight all lands at my end.
opinion dole for 2 : A bowl now can keep a wolf in work long enough for the next bowl to be earned.
opinion sump for 1 : A wolf who knows the first gutter to rise can steer a whole lane home here.
opinion merchants against 2 : Someone who sees a wet coat and raises the price of straw deserves an empty counter.
opinion road mixed 1 : A high road earns its keep when the low one starts floating sticks through the door.
opinion times against 2 [world.times=hard|lean] : It's hard putting a copper by when dinner wants the same copper in advance.

grown
line greet : I'll stand over here where the first drops miss. | Welcome to the higher edge.
line greet.return : I hear you. This little dry spot's free. | A quiet greeting coming back.
line again.open : Here again above the same damp mark.
line farewell : Take the crossing that still shows its stones. | Let the runnel go unacquainted with your feet or purse.
line farewell.return : Safe passage back to your own step. | There's a dry wish to carry away.
line react.news : Give me the first plain bit of the account. | I'll listen where there's a little privacy.
line react.news.new : That hasn't floated past my door before.
line react.news.known : I know which gutter carried that once.
line react.news.doubt : I'd trace that story back to its first damp corner.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : That's more weight than one back ought to carry.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : A bright little mark to set against the day.
line ask.how : Any crossing given you particular trouble today?
line answer.how : Holding level. That's a decent answer for now.
line sympathise : Come where the questions won't crowd you.
line reassure : Even a low sill leaves a bit of dry ground behind it awhile.
line refuse : Some private reckoning of mine finishing first.
line accept_decline : All right. I'll keep the request in my own pocket.
line preclose : I've got a turn to make before my light goes.
line accept_preclose : Go while the high edge is still clear.
line ack : I have the height and direction of it.

scene exchange1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set a straw sideways in a gutter. | I read soaked streets without making much noise.
b : To see the current? | Which signs do you read?
a : To see when the water lifts both ends clear. | The first stem that moves without the wind touching it.

scene exchange2
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the cart along the pier's upper edge. | I learn where a sling was wet by how it dries.
b : Does it roll less? | What's that tell you?
a : A wet plank slopes more than a dry eye expects. | Where the load caught the spray. I turn that side in.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A corner purple with plum makes the best piece of tart. | I save a tart crumb for my walk after work.
b : No plain edge? | How can one crumb be worth saving?
a : A little edge to carry it by, that's all. | It's a taste of something I chose myself.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I see a roof bird put one foot into an eave before both. | I watch the birds choose their roofs after rain.
b : Is that caution? | For worms?
a : Good sense, same as mine at a crossing. | For the first warm tile. I know the waiting.

scene exchange5
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh straw brings a colour into my room that doesn't take a lamp. | I save the straightest new stems from the sweepings.
b : Does it last? | To plait?
a : Till I've walked enough of the street back over it. | To put a line of gold across dark water.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A misty dawn gives the roof birds a second street overhead. | I take the first hour of mist for my own.
b : Where does it show through? | No company wanted?
a : They walk on the ridge and the ridge disappears in mist. | I like one stretch with no explanation owed for the direction I take.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mud won't tell the truth about its depth. | I can cross where the stones break through.
b : What will? | Won't your toes get wet?
a : A stem pushed straight down before a boot. | Toes dry sooner than a whole leg.

scene exchange8
when topic=day self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Night noise travels up through a wall like water through boards. | I like a quiet last hour with a little light.
b : What muffles that sound? | To do your reckoning?
a : I fold dry straw under my pillow and listen to that rustle instead. | Some of it. The dates don't need an audience.

scene exchange9
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I owe money with a date tied to it. | The new moon's got a place in my accounts.
b : Would company help with the figures? | You lend by moonlight?
a : I know its shape too well. I'd rather not give it a louder voice. | Only trying to settle something before the dark bit comes.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could show #self.friend# the high crossing. | A good friend needn't count how many coins I put away.
b : Would you show a stranger too? | Counting for a reason?
a : A crossing's public. What I'm carrying over it can stay private. | Enough of one to do the counting myself.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cargo comes with corners somebody has to walk backwards round. | I lift better when the load comes level before it moves.
b : Is backwards your job? | What if the street's sloping?
a : If the other wolf is steadier at the front, yes. | Then my knees must do the levelling.

scene exchange12
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my saved coin away from market change. | My prices have three columns in my head.
b : A secret pocket? | What are they?
a : A plain one. More important that I remember which is which. | Want it. Need it. Can't until after a certain date.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The talk was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I can't sound its depth. | A story rides a wet street like a straw.
b : Who could? | Do you follow?
a : Somebody who stood there before the words rose up. | I note its direction and let it be carried.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean times leave the saving jar quiet. | When work's thin every late cargo counts.
b : No little clink at all? | Does it pay enough?
a : One sometimes. I'm listening for the next. | A load actually landed is the first thing to count.

scene exchange15
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a say in matching each load to its landing. | One day I'll put a coin aside without promising it to anybody.
b : Like giving orders? | What will you buy?
a : I like knowing why my back's headed one way and not another. | Nothing at first. I'll let it sit in its own right.

scene exchange16
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can draw the Sump in sideways strokes. | The dry way looks crooked from up high.
b : All on a slope? | Is it worth the turns?
a : Each stroke is another level a flood has reached on a wall. | It goes where stone was still showing when I learned it.

scene exchange17
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A damp hip complains before water comes into view. | I pause before straightening with a load.
b : An old knock? | You need a breath?
a : A working shoulder knows its weather too. I protect the two as best I can. | I need to know both feet have a firm opinion under them.

scene exchange18
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't cut through a low court to save ten steps. | I look back at a crossing once I've tested it.
b : Even when it's dry? | Planning to come back?
a : I like remembering one sure route in all weathers. | The safest marker may look different from homeward.

story tale1 [topic=weather]
  : I set a good long straw beside a drain, put a dab of brick on the stone and went to fetch my cloak. Coming back, I found the mark high and dry, the straw gone.
  : I followed a line of little pale ends up the wall with my eyes.
  b : Was the water going uphill?
  : A bird was furnishing a nest. I cut a shorter straw and let the little builder keep the whole long one.

story tale2 [topic=work self.job=sailor]
  : A crate had shifted on the way ashore and its label faced the bottom. I came up with a dozen ways of reading it without turning the load.
  : At last I got down where the gap was and looked upward.
  b : What had they written underneath?
  : This side up. Plenty of room for my face to go hot before anyone saw it.

story tale3 [topic=food self.likes=plum_tart]
  : I ate a purple wedge of tart beside a bowl of water. The last dark crumb dropped in and painted a little purple trail as it sank.
  : I thought for a moment it looked like my whole map of the wet streets.
  b : Which way did it lead?
  : Straight to the bottom. A very short journey for such a lovely last mouthful.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Watch the low corner coming over the plank. | Leave a little dry room for the back foot.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mist on the first roof and the birds already walking. | Pale straw shows up clearly in this light.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That little stem moved without the wind. | Take the upper edge till the water's settled.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A dark corner of tart earns its pastry. | Good plum colour along that cut.
dlg resident.hub : I can spare a private moment on the dry side.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you've found your way to my quiet corner.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late talk carries. Stand close enough to let me speak low.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : There'll be no need to count my pockets to ask a question.
dlg resident.job [self.job=sailor] : I unload where the piers come ashore. The low corner of a load has my attention first.
dlg resident.job : I like a shift that leaves room after it for my own plans.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's what crossed the low streets. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The claim goes #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've no weight to add to it.
dlg resident.bye : Watch the straw before committing your whole boot.

graft resident.hub
choice How much can one straw tell you? -> straw_gauge
node straw_gauge
say Let it lodge sideways and note the waterline below it. If it's gone when you look back, something moved the water or stole the straw.
free
choice How can you tell which? -> straw_gauge_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node straw_gauge_again
say The silt doesn't rise when a bird takes a stem. I look at the mark on the stone as well.
choice I'll watch the next crossing. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
